{
  "abstract": "We study sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples in $(r, \\lambda, S_{ab})$, proving the fifth elements are linear in $S_{ab}$ and cut out the Branch 1 sextuple surface $\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{Br1}}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $\\mathcal{E}_{F_1}, \\mathcal{E}_{F_3}$. Factoring $R_4$ on regular fifths defines $\\mathcal{S}_{4, 2}$, collapsing on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve $\\mathcal{H}$ of relation type $(5, 2)$ with unramified $d = 1$ descent and a new rational almost septuple $\\mathcal{S}_7^{(20/21)}$. In global $(r, \\mu, z)$ coordinates, we construct explicit sextuple families, moving-parameter quintuples on $\\mathcal{E}_B$ (with a $2$-adic period-$6$ lock eliminating $Q_4(k) \\equiv -2$), and the universal triple-square section $L_1 = 0$ of $R_5 = \\frac{L_1 L_2 Q_4}{H K^4}$ with rank-$2$ sublattice $\\Lambda(r) \\subset E(r^2)(\\mathbb{Q}(r))$ and rank-$0$ $E_{16}$ closure at $v = -1/5$. In the $(r, u, v, \\theta)$ chart, we prove the One-$R_5$ Lorentz Syzygy, the Dual Brahmagupta reduction, the 92-term bidegree-$(2,2)$ blow-up $P_{\\text{blowup}}(R, \\omega, \\delta, \\lambda_z) = 0$ with automatic genus-$0$ conics, the root-free Cramer resultant decoder $\\operatorname{Res}_{(P,Q)}(\\mathcal{H}_1, \\mathcal{H}_2) \\equiv (r^2 - 1)N_{\\text{core}}$, and the Universal Vieta Partner linear-$(P, Q)$ splitting into low-degree curves ($C_{9,11}, C_{5,5}^{(g)}, K_{3,3}^{(b)}$) and automatic $20/21$ loci ($\\mathcal{L}_{f,c}^{(u)} = 0, \\mathcal{L}_{g,c}^{(u)} = 0$). On $\\mathcal{S}_{\\text{3-tors}}$, we establish Master Syzygies unifying Family IV, DKMS [7], the Chebyshev elliptic fibration $E_{\\text{Cheb}}(s)$, and $\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{triad}}$ (rank-$0$ $E_{15}$ spoke closure), alongside Mixed-$R_4$ syzygies, $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-2})$ $2$-descent closing $H = 1/3$, Branch B, and paired/antipodal source families and closures. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 19 incorporating the double-point blow-up P_blowup, automatic genus-0 conics, Universal Vieta Partner linear-(P, Q) splitting, and root-free Cramer resultant decoder of exp48, verified in verify_paper.py (exp9-exp48) and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md (Theorem 20(7)) in supplement.zip: (1) 162-Term Quadratic Compression M_quad & 92-Term Bidegree-(2,2) Double-Point Blow-Up P_blowup(R, omega, delta, lambda_z) = 0: Proved that M_core = 0 compresses in (R, delta, psi, sigma_tau) to a 162-term quadratic in sigma_tau (and 114-term quadratic in D_br), and that blowing up the singular double point C_{rat,1}(r) at (z, delta) = (0, 0) via z = lambda_z * delta divides out ((R - 1)*omega + 1)*delta^2 to yield the 92-term bidegree-(2,2) polynomial P_blowup(R, omega, delta, lambda_z) = 0 with completely factored discriminant Delta_{lambda_z}(P_blowup) = 64(2R - 1)^2(4R - omega)^2 k^4 ((R - 1)*omega^2 + 4R)(4k^2 - omega*delta^2), proving both genus-0 conics hold automatically at every non-degenerate rational point and calibrating the ordinary 7-distinct-element 19/21 control (r, u, v) = (53/75, -17/25, -8/25); (2) Root-Free Cramer Resultant Decoder on N_core(r, u, v) = 0: Proved Res_{(P,Q)}(H_1, H_2) == (r^2 - 1)*N_core(r, u, v), so [P : Q] = [-(a_1*c_2 - a_2*c_1) : a_1*b_2 - a_2*b_1], w_1*x_2, C_0, w_1, and x_2 are universally rational at every non-degenerate rational point of N_core = 0; (3) Universal Vieta Partner Linear-(P, Q) Loci, Low-Degree Sub-Regular Curves, and Automatic 20/21 Loci: Proved that for any Y in {a, b, c, d_-, d_+}, R_4(b, d_+, f, Y) and R_4(b, d_+, Y, g) split modulo Q_{1,4} into trivial collisions times linear forms L_{f,Y}^{(v)}(P, Q) and L_{g,Y}^{(v)}(P, Q), yielding the 87-term bidegree-(9,11) curve C_{9,11}(u, v) = 0 (g >= 2) and 105-term C_{10,14}(u, v) = 0 on L_2, the 23-term (5,5) and 31-term (6,5) curves C_{5,5}^{(g)}, C_{6,5}^{(g)} in (r, v) on L_4, the 11-term bidegree-(3,3) curve K_{3,3}^{(b)}(tau_m, u) = 0 on L_8, and the automatic 20/21 loci L_{f,c}^{(u)} = 0 and L_{g,c}^{(u)} = 0 for Y = c.",
